[{"pos":6809,"endPos":7305,"startLine":144,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":153,"endLineOffset":5,"length":497}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":98,"start_side":"RIGHT","start_line":96,"line":98,"comment_lines":["[][96]","[][97]","[][98]"],"review_comment":["Oh, this is very interesting. Thanks for catching this.\r\n\r\nI\u0027m wondering if enforcing unique names for `PhysicalPlan` outputs is actually the right way to go. It is what we assumed so far, so I don\u0027t wanna depart from here, but there\u0027s also a reason to be more lenient:\r\n\r\nIn PhysicalPlan land, this output method was _technically_ correct, because it represented exactly what the physical operators will do: they\u0027re gonna append the blocks for the added fields to the pages that are processed. The blocks corresponding to shadowed attributes/channels will _not_ be stripped from incoming pages.\r\n\r\nThis means that the output layout technically has duplicate attribute names. This change just hides them and makes them inaccessible during the physical planning stage.\r\n\r\nFWIW, `EvalExec` has the exact same situation. `Eval` performs shadowing, but `EvalOperator` can only ever append blocks, so the output pages actually still contain the blocks corresponding to shadowed attributes."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/LookupJoinExec.java","id":36728,"created_at":"2024-12-10T10:51:47Z","original_position":9,"side":"RIGHT","position":9,"original_start_line":96,"submitted_on_commit":"d3b3dc627eaf45d3a255b1e3e5293fc31b395231","diff_hunk":"@@ -93,9 +93,9 @@ public List\u003cAttribute\u003e addedFields() {\n     public List\u003cAttribute\u003e output() {\n         if (lazyOutput \u003d\u003d null) {\n             lazyOutput \u003d new ArrayList\u003c\u003e(left().output());\n-            for (Attribute attr : addedFields) {\n-                lazyOutput.add(attr);\n-            }\n+            var addedFieldsNames \u003d addedFields.stream().map(Attribute::name).toList();\n+            lazyOutput.removeIf(a -\u003e addedFieldsNames.contains(a.name()));\n+            lazyOutput.addAll(addedFields);","submitted_start_line":96,"submitted_line":98},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The logic in `output` method of `LookupJoinExec` has been modified to remove attributes from `lazyOutput` if their names match any name in `addedFields`. This could lead to incorrect behavior if there are attributes with the same name but different meanings. Consider using attribute IDs or other unique identifiers instead of just names.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/LookupJoinExec.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/LookupJoinExec.java-3425:3513-3425:3499,3512:3574,3587:3618","promptId":"#1NCJM","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/LookupJoinExec.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/LookupJoinExec.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":3425,"endPos":3513,"startLine":96,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":98,"endLineOffset":13,"length":89}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3425,"endPos":3499,"startLine":96,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":96,"endLineOffset":86,"length":75},{"pos":3512,"endPos":3574,"startLine":97,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":97,"endLineOffset":74,"length":63},{"pos":3587,"endPos":3618,"startLine":98,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":98,"endLineOffset":43,"length":32}]}]}]}],"coveredGroundTruth":1,"uncoveredGroundTruth":0,"coveredMatchable":9,"uncoveredMatchable":28,"timing":61617,"tokensIn":12024,"tokensOut":847}